    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `contactPreference` field surfaces on `GET /api/owners/{id}`, whose `OwnerDto` is generated from the OpenAPI spec and populated by MapStruct.\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` that derives the value via a new helper:\n   ```java\n   protected String contactPreference(Owner owner) {\n       return (owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isEmpty()) ? \"EMAIL\" : \"PHONE\";\n   }\n   ```\n   This mirrors the existing `membershipLevel` email-presence check (null or empty email \u2192 `PHONE`, otherwise `EMAIL`).\n\nBoth new acceptance tests pass: `PHONE` when no email is present, `EMAIL` when one is.",
